{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-65229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-65229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-65229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6a11bbc8e45b433d43fed22e4ec987c6a991fc9ce8b5659acbd652964558b73b"} {"question" "q-65229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-65229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-65229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the trigonometric expression ${cos}^{3}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{5}⁡\\theta .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{5}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{3}⁡\\theta ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & ={cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{5}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{3}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6a11bbc8e45b433d43fed22e4ec987c6a991fc9ce8b5659acbd652964558b73b"} {"question" "q-119362" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119362" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "2+{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "2{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119362" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ from the first two terms of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot 1+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+{(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6a11bbc8e45b433d43fed22e4ec987c6a991fc9ce8b5659acbd652964558b73b"} {"question" "q-119392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119767" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6a11bbc8e45b433d43fed22e4ec987c6a991fc9ce8b5659acbd652964558b73b"} {"question" "q-119767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119767" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1}-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6a11bbc8e45b433d43fed22e4ec987c6a991fc9ce8b5659acbd652964558b73b"} {"question" "q-119775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981447/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae520db5e67c0a68c57bf371b51bf2656f0da9ad49bc9f7f3228c59e367f7016"} {"question" "q-119775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correc